        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slow cooling at approximately 52 K/s produces a complex microstructure containing multiple crystalline phases.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Accelerated cooling at approximately 3018 K/s reduces the number of crystalline phases but still yields primarily FCC A and tetragonal D phases.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt spinning can cool this alloy at 10^5–10^6 K/s.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A melt-spun ribbon thickness of approximately 20 µm contributes to achieving the stated rapid-cooling conditions.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The melt-spinning process should be performed under an inert atmosphere.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid cooling induces undercooling that kinetically suppresses nucleation of primary non-eutectic phases and leads to a predominantly amorphous structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods",
        "PMC11642357::web::017::4_discussion",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 10^5–10^6 K/s there is insufficient time for atoms to rearrange into ordered crystalline phases.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid cooling overcomes the thermodynamic driving forces for crystallization, especially for phosphorus-poor phases.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Phosphorus and high mixing entropy promote glass formation in this alloy during extremely rapid cooling.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very rapid cooling by melt spinning yields an amorphous structure in this alloy, as assessed by XRD and TEM.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The melt-spun alloy will have higher thermal stability during subsequent reheating than the 52 K/s and 3018 K/s samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The melt-spun alloy will crystallize in a single step or through a simplified sequence upon reheating.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved thermal stability will be evidenced by reduced and shifted exothermic crystallization peaks during reheating.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The improvement is expected above an approximate cooling-rate threshold of 10^5 K/s.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cooling rates at or below approximately 3018 K/s can still permit substantial primary crystallization.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::010::2_materials_and_methods",
        "PMC11642357::web::021::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "FCC crystallization shifts from approximately 1706 K under slow cooling to approximately 1341 K under accelerated cooling.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::017::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The 1706 K to 1341 K shift provides a boundary for the melt-spun alloy's crystallization behavior during subsequent reheating.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11642357::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC11642357::web::017::4_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of thermal-stability enhancement and the completeness of phase suppression may depend on ribbon thickness, inert-gas flow, phosphorus content, and mixing entropy.",
